x = \frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \quad y = \frac{y_1 + y_2}{2}
\]
Substituting the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$, we get \[
x = \frac{5 + (-3)}{2}, \quad y = \frac{3 + 6}{2}
\]
\[
x = \frac{2}{2}, \quad y = \frac{9}{2}
\]
\[
x = 1, \quad y = \frac{9}{2}
\]
